/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Matthew chapters 21-25
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("matthew", [
{n:21, name:"The Triumphal Entry",
 seal:{ref:"Matthew 21:9",verse:"And the multitudes that went before, and that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna to the Son of David: Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord; Hosanna in the highest."},
 facts:["Did you know 'Hosanna' is a Hebrew cry meaning 'save us now,' first prayed in Psalm 118 and turned by the crowds into a shout of royal praise (Matthew 21:9)?","Did you know Matthew alone notes both the ass and her colt, matching Zechariah's prophecy word for word, 'an ass, and a colt the foal of an ass' (Matthew 21:5)?","Did you know Jesus answered his critics with their own Scriptures, quoting Psalm 8 about praise from babes and Psalm 118 about the rejected stone (Matthew 21:16, 42)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"How many disciples did Jesus send ahead to the village?", options:["Two","Three","Ten","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:1",verse:"And when they drew nigh unto Jerusalem, and were come to Bethphage, unto the mount of Olives, then sent Jesus two disciples,", insight:"Two disciples, one simple errand; the greatest week in history began with an ordinary act of obedience."},
{q:"What did Jesus say they would find tied in the village?", options:["An ass tied, and a colt with her","A pair of oxen under a yoke","A white horse with a saddle","Two lambs for the offering"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:2",verse:"Saying unto them, Go into the village over against you, and straightway ye shall find an ass tied, and a colt with her: loose them, and bring them unto me.", insight:"He described it exactly before they saw it; nothing about that week caught Jesus by surprise."},
{q:"What were the disciples to say if anyone questioned them?", options:["The Lord hath need of them","The Master commands it","We will return them by evening","The temple requires them"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:3",verse:"And if any man say ought unto you, ye shall say, The Lord hath need of them; and straightway he will send them.", insight:"'The Lord hath need of them' was answer enough; when God asks for what is ours, trust is the whole reason."},
{q:"How did the prophecy describe the coming King?", options:["Meek, and sitting upon an ass, and a colt the foal of an ass","Mighty, riding a war horse to battle","Crowned in gold, carried on a throne","Hidden, walking barefoot with the poor"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:5",verse:"Tell ye the daughter of Sion, Behold, thy King cometh unto thee, meek, and sitting upon an ass, and a colt the foal of an ass.", insight:"Meek on a donkey, not fierce on a charger; God's power arrives in humility."},
{q:"What did the very great multitude spread in the way?", options:["Their garments, and branches cut from the trees","Woven carpets and silk banners","Palm fronds gathered in bundles","Grain and firstfruits of the field"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:8",verse:"And a very great multitude spread their garments in the way; others cut down branches from the trees, and strawed them in the way.", insight:"Coats off their backs and branches from the trees; real worship gives what it has."},
{q:"What did the multitudes cry as they went before and followed him?", options:["Hosanna to the Son of David: Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord","Blessed be the King of the Jews forever","Glory to God in the highest heaven","Peace on earth, good will to men"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:9",verse:"And the multitudes that went before, and that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna to the Son of David: Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord; Hosanna in the highest.", insight:"Hosanna means 'save us now'; the crowd named its deepest need in the middle of its praise."},
{q:"When the city asked 'Who is this?', how did the multitude answer?", options:["This is Jesus the prophet of Nazareth of Galilee","This is Jesus the son of Joseph","This is the Messiah, the Son of David","This is the teacher from Bethany"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:11",verse:"And the multitude said, This is Jesus the prophet of Nazareth of Galilee.", insight:"'Prophet of Nazareth' was true but too small; people can see Jesus clearly and still miss his full glory."},
{q:"What did Jesus overthrow when he entered the temple?", options:["The tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves","The altar of burnt offering","The seven-branched candlesticks","The chests of the treasury"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:12",verse:"And Jesus went into the temple of God, and cast out all them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves,", insight:"Zeal for God's house moved him to act; some tables deserve to be overturned."},
{q:"Jesus said his house should be called a house of prayer, but they had made it what?", options:["A den of thieves","A marketplace of the nations","A court of bargaining","A hall of money"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:13",verse:"And said unto them, It is written, My house shall be called the house of prayer; but ye have made it a den of thieves.", insight:"Worship had become business; Jesus draws a hard line between devotion and profit."},
{q:"Who came to Jesus in the temple after the cleansing?", options:["The blind and the lame came, and he healed them","The lepers came, and he cleansed them","The possessed came, and he freed them","The poor came, and he fed them"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:14",verse:"And the blind and the lame came to him in the temple; and he healed them.", insight:"Cleansing came first, then healing; when the house is pure, mercy flows freely."},
{q:"When the priests complained about the children's praise, what Scripture did Jesus quote?", options:["Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings thou hast perfected praise","The stone the builders rejected is become the head of the corner","I will have mercy, and not sacrifice","Blessed are the pure in heart"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:16",verse:"And said unto him, Hearest thou what these say? And Jesus saith unto them, Yea; have ye never read, Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings thou hast perfected praise?", insight:"God perfects praise from children's mouths; the simple often see what the learned resist."},
{q:"When Jesus came to the fig tree, what did he find?", options:["Nothing thereon, but leaves only","Figs not yet ripe","A withered root","Fruit hidden under the leaves"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:19",verse:"And when he saw a fig tree in the way, he came to it, and found nothing thereon, but leaves only, and said unto it, Let no fruit grow on thee henceforward for ever. And presently the fig tree withered away.", insight:"Leaves without fruit are religion without life; Jesus looks past the show for the harvest."},
{q:"What did Jesus say undoubting faith could command?", options:["Say to this mountain, Be thou removed, and be thou cast into the sea, and it shall be done","Command the fig tree to bear fruit in winter","Speak, and the temple would be rebuilt","Call down bread from heaven"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:21",verse:"Jesus answered and said unto them, Verily I say unto you, If ye have faith, and doubt not, ye shall not only do this which is done to the fig tree, but also if ye shall say unto this mountain, Be thou removed, and be thou cast into the sea; it shall be done.", insight:"Faith that does not doubt moves mountains; the size of the obstacle never limits God."},
{q:"What did Jesus promise about asking in prayer?", options:["All things, whatsoever ye shall ask in prayer, believing, ye shall receive","Only small things shall be granted","Ask in the temple, and it shall be given","Prayer is heard when many gather"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:22",verse:"And all things, whatsoever ye shall ask in prayer, believing, ye shall receive.", insight:"Believing is the hinge of the promise; prayer is not wishing, it is trusting."},
{q:"What single question did Jesus put to the priests about John?", options:["The baptism of John, whence was it? from heaven, or of men?","Was John greater than Elijah?","Did John baptize in the Jordan?","Why did you not follow John?"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:25",verse:"The baptism of John, whence was it? from heaven, or of men? And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say unto us, Why did ye not then believe him?", insight:"One honest question exposed their fear of the crowd; evasion is often the mark of a trapped conscience."},
{q:"Why would the priests not say John's baptism was 'of men'?", options:["They feared the people; for all hold John as a prophet","They truly did not know","The law forbade them to judge","They had never met John"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:26",verse:"But if we shall say, Of men; we fear the people; for all hold John as a prophet.", insight:"Fear of the crowd, not love of truth, steered their answer; popularity is a poor compass."},
{q:"In the parable of the two sons, what did the first son do?", options:["He said, I will not: but afterward he repented, and went","He said, I go, sir: and went not","He asked for his wages first","He sent his brother in his place"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:29",verse:"He answered and said, I will not: but afterward he repented, and went.", insight:"The son who said no but repented did the father's will; a changed life outweighs a polite word."},
{q:"Who did Jesus say would enter the kingdom of God before the priests?", options:["The publicans and the harlots","The Romans and the Greeks","The scribes and the Pharisees","The rich and the rulers"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:31",verse:"Whether of them twain did the will of his father? They say unto him, The first. Jesus saith unto them, Verily I say unto you, That the publicans and the harlots go into the kingdom of God before you.", insight:"Repentant sinners outran the religious leaders; heaven's door opens to the broken, not the proud."},
{q:"When the husbandmen saw the son, what did they say among themselves?", options:["This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and let us seize on his inheritance","This is the heir; let us honor him","This is a servant; let us beat him","This is the lord; let us hide"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:38",verse:"But when the husbandmen saw the son, they said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and let us seize on his inheritance.", insight:"They knew exactly who he was and killed him anyway; the darkest sin is the deliberate kind."},
{q:"Which Scripture did Jesus quote about the rejected stone?", options:["The stone which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner","I will build my church upon this rock","The Lord is my shepherd","A stone cut out without hands"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 21:42",verse:"Jesus saith unto them, Did ye never read in the scriptures, The stone which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner: this is the Lord’s doing, and it is marvellous in our eyes?", insight:"The rejected stone became the cornerstone; what men discard, God makes the foundation."}
]},
{n:22, name:"The Wedding Feast",
 seal:{ref:"Matthew 22:37",verse:"Jesus said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind."},
 facts:["Did you know the 'penny' of Matthew 22:19 was a denarius, a full day's wage for a laborer, and it bore the image of Tiberius Caesar?","Did you know the Sadducees accepted only the five books of Moses, which is why Jesus proved the resurrection from Exodus, a book they could not dismiss (Matthew 22:32)?","Did you know many scholars note that wedding garments were often supplied by the host, which would make the garmentless guest's refusal deliberate rather than a matter of poverty (Matthew 22:11)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"To what did Jesus liken the kingdom of heaven?", options:["A certain king, which made a marriage for his son","A merchant seeking goodly pearls","A shepherd with a hundred sheep","A sower who went forth to sow"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:2",verse:"The kingdom of heaven is like unto a certain king, which made a marriage for his son,", insight:"The kingdom is a wedding feast; God invites us to joy, not drudgery."},
{q:"How did those who were bidden answer the king's invitation?", options:["They made light of it, and went their ways, one to his farm, another to his merchandise","They came at once with gifts","They sent letters of excuse","They asked for another day"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:5",verse:"But they made light of it, and went their ways, one to his farm, another to his merchandise:", insight:"They did not hate the feast; they just preferred the farm. Indifference can be as deadly as hostility."},
{q:"What did the angry king do to the murderers of his servants?", options:["He sent forth his armies, and destroyed those murderers, and burned up their city","He forgave them and sent again","He fined them double the tax","He banished them from the land"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:7",verse:"But when the king heard thereof, he was wroth: and he sent forth his armies, and destroyed those murderers, and burned up their city.", insight:"Spiteful rejection of grace has consequences; even the king's patience has an end."},
{q:"Where did the king send his servants to find new guests?", options:["Into the highways","Into the villages of Galilee","To the gates of the city","To the houses of the rich"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:9",verse:"Go ye therefore into the highways, and as many as ye shall find, bid to the marriage.", insight:"The highways filled the hall; God's guest list reaches the overlooked and the passerby."},
{q:"Whom did the servants gather from the highways?", options:["Both bad and good","Only the poor","Only the righteous","Only the king's friends"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:10",verse:"So those servants went out into the highways, and gathered together all as many as they found, both bad and good: and the wedding was furnished with guests.", insight:"Bad and good alike were bid; the invitation is wide, but the garment still matters."},
{q:"What was wrong with the man the king noticed among the guests?", options:["He had not on a wedding garment","He had stolen food from the table","He sat in the king's own seat","He refused to eat or drink"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:11",verse:"And when the king came in to see the guests, he saw there a man which had not on a wedding garment:", insight:"He came to the feast but not dressed for it; grace invites us, but we must come on God's terms."},
{q:"What was done with the man without a wedding garment?", options:["Bind him hand and foot, and cast him into outer darkness","He was sent out to buy a garment","He was seated at the lowest place","He was fined and released"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:13",verse:"Then said the king to the servants, Bind him hand and foot, and take him away, and cast him into outer darkness; there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.", insight:"Speechless before the king, he had no excuse; presumption has no answer at the judgment."},
{q:"How did Jesus sum up the parable?", options:["For many are called, but few are chosen","The last shall be first","Blessed are the meek","The kingdom suffers violence"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:14",verse:"For many are called, but few are chosen.", insight:"Many hear the call; few are chosen. The difference is in how we answer."},
{q:"Whom did the Pharisees send out with their disciples to entangle Jesus?", options:["The Herodians","The Sadducees","The Roman soldiers","The publicans"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:16",verse:"And they sent out unto him their disciples with the Herodians, saying, Master, we know that thou art true, and teachest the way of God in truth, neither carest thou for any man: for thou regardest not the person of men.", insight:"Pharisees and Herodians were enemies, yet they united against Jesus; opposition to Christ makes strange allies."},
{q:"What trap question did they put to Jesus about tribute?", options:["Is it lawful to give tribute unto Caesar, or not?","Should the temple tax be doubled?","Must Jews pay the priests first?","Is Caesar greater than God?"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:17",verse:"Tell us therefore, What thinkest thou? Is it lawful to give tribute unto Caesar, or not?", insight:"Either answer seemed fatal; flattery opened the trap, but wisdom walked straight through it."},
{q:"What did Jesus ask them to show him?", options:["The tribute money","Their purses and bags","The tax records","A talent of silver"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:19",verse:"Shew me the tribute money. And they brought unto him a penny.", insight:"He asked for the coin they carried; the trap was sprung with their own money."},
{q:"What was Jesus' answer about Caesar and God?", options:["Render therefore unto Caesar the things which are Caesar's; and unto God the things that are God's","Give everything to Caesar, for he is lord","Refuse Caesar, and serve God only","Flee the tax, for the kingdom is near"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:21",verse:"They say unto him, Caesar’s. Then saith he unto them, Render therefore unto Caesar the things which are Caesar’s; and unto God the things that are God’s.", insight:"Caesar's image was stamped on the coin; God's image is stamped on us, and we are owed to him."},
{q:"Which group came to Jesus denying that there is a resurrection?", options:["The Sadducees","The Essenes","The Zealots","The Samaritans"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:23",verse:"The same day came to him the Sadducees, which say that there is no resurrection, and asked him,", insight:"They denied the resurrection and then argued about it; unbelief still has to face its own questions."},
{q:"In the Sadducees' puzzle, how many brothers married the same woman in turn?", options:["Seven","Five","Three","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:25",verse:"Now there were with us seven brethren: and the first, when he had married a wife, deceased, and, having no issue, left his wife unto his brother:", insight:"Seven brothers, one riddle; they thought marriage law could stump the Author of life."},
{q:"Why did Jesus say the Sadducees erred?", options:["Not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God","Not honoring Moses","Not fearing the priests","Not keeping the Sabbath"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:29",verse:"Jesus answered and said unto them, Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God.", insight:"Ignorance of Scripture and doubt of God's power; the two roots of most error are still these."},
{q:"What did Jesus teach about marriage in the resurrection?", options:["They neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of God in heaven","All shall be married to Christ","Marriage continues forever","Only the righteous shall marry"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:30",verse:"For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of God in heaven.", insight:"Heaven is not earth extended; the resurrection life is fuller, not smaller."},
{q:"How did Jesus prove the resurrection from God's own words?", options:["I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob: God is not the God of the dead, but of the living","The dead shall hear the voice of the Son of God","Thy dead men shall live together","I am the resurrection, and the life"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:32",verse:"I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob? God is not the God of the dead, but of the living.", insight:"'I am,' not 'I was'; to God the patriarchs are alive, and so shall we be."},
{q:"What is the first and great commandment?", options:["Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind","Thou shalt not kill","Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy","Honour thy father and thy mother"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:37",verse:"Jesus said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind.", insight:"All of God with all of us; love is the whole law gathered into one command."},
{q:"What is the second commandment, like unto the first?", options:["Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself","Thou shalt not steal","Thou shalt not bear false witness","Thou shalt not covet"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:39",verse:"And the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.", insight:"Love of God spills into love of neighbor; the vertical always shapes the horizontal."},
{q:"In the psalm Jesus quoted, what does the LORD say to David's Lord?", options:["Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool","Thou art a priest for ever","Rule thou in the midst of thine enemies","I have set my king upon my holy hill"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 22:44",verse:"The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool?", insight:"David called his own son 'Lord'; the Messiah is greater than his ancestry."}
]},
{n:23, name:"Woe to the Pharisees",
 seal:{ref:"Matthew 23:37",verse:"O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, thou that killest the prophets, and stonest them which are sent unto thee, how often would I have gathered thy children together, even as a hen gathereth her chickens under her wings, and ye would not!"},
 facts:["Did you know phylacteries were small leather boxes holding Scripture texts, worn on the arm and forehead from Deuteronomy 6, which the Pharisees made extra broad to be noticed (Matthew 23:5)?","Did you know 'strain at a gnat' pictures filtering wine through cloth to avoid an unclean insect, while the camel, the largest unclean animal, went down whole (Matthew 23:24)?","Did you know 'from the blood of Abel unto the blood of Zacharias' spans the whole Hebrew Bible, from the first murder in Genesis to the last recorded one in 2 Chronicles, the final book of the Hebrew canon (Matthew 23:35)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"Who did Jesus say sit in Moses' seat?", options:["The scribes and the Pharisees","The chief priests and elders","The Sadducees and Herodians","The lawyers and doctors"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:2",verse:"Saying, The scribes and the Pharisees sit in Moses’ seat:", insight:"They held Moses' office; Jesus honored the seat even as he exposed the sitters."},
{q:"What did Jesus tell the people to do about the Pharisees' teaching?", options:["Observe and do what they bid, but do not follow their works, for they say, and do not","Reject everything they teach","Follow their example in all things","Leave the synagogues at once"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:3",verse:"All therefore whatsoever they bid you observe, that observe and do; but do not ye after their works: for they say, and do not.", insight:"Truth is truth even from flawed lips; but example matters, and theirs failed the test."},
{q:"What did they lay on men's shoulders?", options:["Heavy burdens grievous to be borne, which they themselves would not move with one of their fingers","A doubled temple tax","Fasting three days every week","Stones for the city wall"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:4",verse:"For they bind heavy burdens and grievous to be borne, and lay them on men’s shoulders; but they themselves will not move them with one of their fingers.", insight:"They loaded others and lifted nothing themselves; leadership that will not lift is tyranny."},
{q:"What did they broaden and enlarge to be seen of men?", options:["Their phylacteries, and the borders of their garments","Their houses and their gates","Their scrolls and their seals","Their tables and their couches"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:5",verse:"But all their works they do for to be seen of men: they make broad their phylacteries, and enlarge the borders of their garments,", insight:"Bigger borders, smaller hearts; showiness is the tell of a hollow religion."},
{q:"What places did they love at feasts and in the synagogues?", options:["The uppermost rooms at feasts, and the chief seats in the synagogues","The lowest seats with the poor","The outer courts with the Gentiles","The seats nearest the door"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:6",verse:"And love the uppermost rooms at feasts, and the chief seats in the synagogues,", insight:"They loved the best seats; humility takes the low place and lets God do the exalting."},
{q:"Why were the disciples not to be called Rabbi?", options:["For one is your Master, even Christ; and all ye are brethren","For the title belongs to Moses alone","For no man is worthy of it","For the Romans had forbidden it"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:8",verse:"But be not ye called Rabbi: for one is your Master, even Christ; and all ye are brethren.", insight:"One Master, all brethren; in Christ's school there are no ranked thrones."},
{q:"Who is the greatest among Christ's followers?", options:["He that is greatest among you shall be your servant","He who knows the most Scripture","He who gives the most alms","He who prays the longest prayers"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:11",verse:"But he that is greatest among you shall be your servant.", insight:"Greatness serves; the towel, not the title, marks the greatest."},
{q:"What happens to the one who exalts himself?", options:["He shall be abased; and he that shall humble himself shall be exalted","He shall be honored by men","He shall lead the synagogue","He shall be made a ruler"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:12",verse:"And whosoever shall exalt himself shall be abased; and he that shall humble himself shall be exalted.", insight:"God's scale runs upside down from ours; the way up is down."},
{q:"How many 'woe' pronouncements does Jesus speak against the scribes and Pharisees in this chapter?", options:["Eight","Seven","Six","Ten"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:13",verse:"But woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye shut up the kingdom of heaven against men: for ye neither go in yourselves, neither suffer ye them that are entering to go in.", insight:"Eight woes, each aimed at a specific hypocrisy; Jesus is thorough because the disease is thorough."},
{q:"What did they devour while making long prayers for a pretence?", options:["Widows' houses","The temple treasury","The tithes of the poor","The offerings of strangers"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:14",verse:"Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye devour widows’ houses, and for a pretence make long prayer: therefore ye shall receive the greater damnation.", insight:"Long prayers covering theft; piety that preys on the weak draws the greater damnation."},
{q:"What did they do with a single proselyte?", options:["They compassed sea and land to make him, then made him twofold more the child of hell than themselves","They taught him the law perfectly","They brought him to the temple","They made him a scribe"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:15",verse:"Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye compass sea and land to make one proselyte, and when he is made, ye make him twofold more the child of hell than yourselves.", insight:"Zeal without truth multiplies the damage; a convert to error is worse off than before."},
{q:"What did these blind guides teach about swearing?", options:["Swearing by the temple is nothing, but swearing by the gold of the temple makes a man a debtor","All oaths are utterly forbidden","Swear only by heaven above","The temple oath is the greatest"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:16",verse:"Woe unto you, ye blind guides, which say, Whosoever shall swear by the temple, it is nothing; but whosoever shall swear by the gold of the temple, he is a debtor!", insight:"They valued the gold above the house that sanctified it; misplaced values make blind guides."},
{q:"What small things did they tithe with great care?", options:["Mint and anise and cummin","Wheat and barley and oil","Gold and silver and spices","Sheep and oxen and doves"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:23",verse:"Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye pay tithe of mint and anise and cummin, and have omitted the weightier matters of the law, judgment, mercy, and faith: these ought ye to have done, and not to leave the other undone.", insight:"They counted herbs and skipped justice; small exactness never excuses great neglect."},
{q:"What weightier matters of the law had they omitted?", options:["Judgment, mercy, and faith","Prayer, fasting, and alms","Sabbath, circumcision, and Passover","Love, joy, and peace"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:23",verse:"Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye pay tithe of mint and anise and cummin, and have omitted the weightier matters of the law, judgment, mercy, and faith: these ought ye to have done, and not to leave the other undone.", insight:"Judgment, mercy, and faith are the weight of the law; everything else is garnish."},
{q:"What biting picture did Jesus paint of their fussiness?", options:["They strain at a gnat, and swallow a camel","They build their house on sand","They are wolves in sheep's clothing","They are clouds without water"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:24",verse:"Ye blind guides, which strain at a gnat, and swallow a camel.", insight:"Straining gnats while swallowing camels; fussiness over trifles with blindness to enormity."},
{q:"To what did Jesus compare them in the woe about the cup?", options:["They clean the outside of the cup and platter, but within are full of extortion and excess","They are whited sepulchres","They are blind guides","They are painted tombs"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:25",verse:"Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye make clean the outside of the cup and of the platter, but within they are full of extortion and excess.", insight:"Clean outside, corrupt within; God starts the washing on the inside."},
{q:"What are they like, beautiful outward but full of dead men's bones within?", options:["Whited sepulchres","Painted temples","Gilded altars","Washed tombs of kings"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:27",verse:"Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead men’s bones, and of all uncleanness.", insight:"Whitewash on a grave; a fair appearance can be the most expensive lie."},
{q:"What did Jesus say they witnessed against themselves?", options:["That they are the children of them which killed the prophets","That they are strangers to the covenant","That they are blind guides","That they are friends of Rome"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:31",verse:"Wherefore ye be witnesses unto yourselves, that ye are the children of them which killed the prophets.", insight:"Their own words condemned them; we often testify against ourselves."},
{q:"What did Jesus call them when he asked how they could escape hell?", options:["Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers","Ye wolves of the field","Ye blind hypocrites","Ye sons of thunder"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:33",verse:"Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of hell?", insight:"Serpents and vipers; Jesus named the danger plainly because the stakes were eternal."},
{q:"How did Jesus describe his longing to gather Jerusalem?", options:["Even as a hen gathereth her chickens under her wings, and ye would not","As a shepherd seeks his lost sheep","As a father waits for his son","As an eagle bears her young"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 23:37",verse:"O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, thou that killest the prophets, and stonest them which are sent unto thee, how often would I have gathered thy children together, even as a hen gathereth her chickens under her wings, and ye would not!", insight:"A hen's wings against the storm; his heart broke over the city that would not come."}
]},
{n:24, name:"The Olivet Discourse",
 seal:{ref:"Matthew 24:35",verse:"Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away."},
 facts:["Did you know Jesus' 'not one stone upon another' was fulfilled in AD 70, when the Romans destroyed the temple so thoroughly that stones were pried apart for the gold melted between them (Matthew 24:2)?","Did you know 'this generation shall not pass' (Matthew 24:34) is one of the most debated verses in the Bible, with many understanding 'generation' as the Jewish people enduring until all is fulfilled?","Did you know the 'abomination of desolation' (Matthew 24:15) reaches back to Daniel 9 and 11, and Jesus adds the aside 'whoso readeth, let him understand,' urging careful study?"],
 questions:[
{q:"As Jesus left the temple, what did the disciples come to show him?", options:["The buildings of the temple","The golden gate","The treasury chests","The new outer courts"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:1",verse:"And Jesus went out, and departed from the temple: and his disciples came to him for to shew him the buildings of the temple.", insight:"They admired the stones; he saw their future. Buildings impress us; God looks at what lasts."},
{q:"What did Jesus say would happen to the temple stones?", options:["There shall not be left here one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down","They shall be covered with gold","They shall stand until his return","They shall be carried away to Rome"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:2",verse:"And Jesus said unto them, See ye not all these things? verily I say unto you, There shall not be left here one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down.", insight:"Not one stone upon another; even the grandest human work falls on schedule."},
{q:"Where was Jesus sitting when the disciples asked him privately?", options:["Upon the mount of Olives","In the temple courts","Beside the Sea of Galilee","On a housetop"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:3",verse:"And as he sat upon the mount of Olives, the disciples came unto him privately, saying, Tell us, when shall these things be? and what shall be the sign of thy coming, and of the end of the world?", insight:"They came privately with big questions; Jesus welcomes honest curiosity about the future."},
{q:"What did the disciples ask Jesus on the mount of Olives?", options:["When shall these things be? and what shall be the sign of thy coming, and of the end of the world?","When will the temple be rebuilt, and Rome defeated?","Where will the kingdom's capital stand?","Who will sit at thy right hand?"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:3",verse:"And as he sat upon the mount of Olives, the disciples came unto him privately, saying, Tell us, when shall these things be? and what shall be the sign of thy coming, and of the end of the world?", insight:"They linked the temple's fall with the end of the world; Jesus untangled the near from the far."},
{q:"What was Jesus' first warning about the last days?", options:["Take heed that no man deceive you","Flee to the mountains at once","Sell all that you have","Hide in the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:4",verse:"And Jesus answered and said unto them, Take heed that no man deceive you.", insight:"Deception heads his list of end-time dangers; discernment is the first survival skill."},
{q:"What did Jesus say about wars and rumours of wars?", options:["See that ye be not troubled: for all these things must come to pass, but the end is not yet","They are the final and certain sign","Flee the cities when you hear them","They will all end within a year"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:6",verse:"And ye shall hear of wars and rumours of wars: see that ye be not troubled: for all these things must come to pass, but the end is not yet.", insight:"Wars alarm us, but they are not the end; troubled hearts need his steadying word."},
{q:"Besides nation rising against nation, what troubles did Jesus name?", options:["Famines, and pestilences, and earthquakes, in divers places","Floods, and fires, and storms","Darkness, and hail, and plagues","Drought, and locusts, and wild beasts"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:7",verse:"For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be famines, and pestilences, and earthquakes, in divers places.", insight:"Nature groans along with the nations; creation itself feels the weight of the age."},
{q:"What did Jesus call all these early troubles?", options:["The beginning of sorrows","The great tribulation","The day of wrath","The final hour"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:8",verse:"All these are the beginning of sorrows.", insight:"Birth pangs, not the birth; the worst is not yet, and neither is the best."},
{q:"According to Jesus, who shall be saved?", options:["He that shall endure unto the end","He that flees the earliest","He that hides the deepest","He that learns every sign"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:13",verse:"But he that shall endure unto the end, the same shall be saved.", insight:"Endurance, not excitement, is the mark; finishing matters more than starting."},
{q:"What must be preached in all the world before the end comes?", options:["This gospel of the kingdom, for a witness unto all nations","The rebuilding of the temple","The keeping of the Sabbath","The fall of Rome"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:14",verse:"And this gospel of the kingdom shall be preached in all the world for a witness unto all nations; and then shall the end come.", insight:"The gospel to all nations is the clock of the end; missions hasten his coming."},
{q:"What sign did Jesus say Daniel the prophet spoke of?", options:["The abomination of desolation, standing in the holy place","The drying of the great river","The falling of the stars","The sealing of the book"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:15",verse:"When ye therefore shall see the abomination of desolation, spoken of by Daniel the prophet, stand in the holy place, (whoso readeth, let him understand:)", insight:"Daniel's old prophecy becomes the signal; Scripture interprets the headlines."},
{q:"When they see that sign, where should those in Judaea flee?", options:["Into the mountains","Into Egypt","Across the Jordan","Into the temple"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:16",verse:"Then let them which be in Judaea flee into the mountains:", insight:"When the sign appears, run; obedience in that hour is urgent and simple."},
{q:"What did Jesus tell them to pray about their flight?", options:["That it be not in the winter, neither on the sabbath day","That they have food for the way","That the Romans show mercy","That the city gates stay open"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:20",verse:"But pray ye that your flight be not in the winter, neither on the sabbath day:", insight:"He cares about the details of our hardship; even escape plans deserve prayer."},
{q:"What will false Christs and false prophets show?", options:["Great signs and wonders, so as to deceive, if possible, the very elect","New scriptures and new laws","Armies and weapons of war","Gold and riches untold"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:24",verse:"For there shall arise false Christs, and false prophets, and shall shew great signs and wonders; insomuch that, if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect.", insight:"Miracles can mislead; wonder-working is no proof of truth."},
{q:"How did Jesus describe the manner of his coming?", options:["As the lightning cometh out of the east, and shineth even unto the west","As a thief breaking in at night","As a king on a white horse","As a still, small voice"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:27",verse:"For as the lightning cometh out of the east, and shineth even unto the west; so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.", insight:"Lightning needs no announcement; his return will be unmistakable to all."},
{q:"How will the Son of man appear?", options:["In the clouds of heaven with power and great glory","On foot through the desert","In secret within the temple","As a child in Bethlehem"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:30",verse:"And then shall appear the sign of the Son of man in heaven: and then shall all the tribes of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of man coming in the clouds of heaven with power and great glory.", insight:"Clouds, power, great glory; the humble entry is past, the glorious return is ahead."},
{q:"What will the angels do at his coming?", options:["Gather his elect from the four winds with a great sound of a trumpet","Pour out vials of wrath","Seal the tribes of Israel","Bind Satan for a thousand years"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:31",verse:"And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.", insight:"A trumpet and a gathering; the end is not a scattering but a homecoming."},
{q:"What did Jesus say about heaven, earth, and his words?", options:["Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away","Heaven and earth shall be renewed together","My words shall be sealed until the end","The earth abides forever"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:35",verse:"Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.", insight:"Worlds pass; his words do not. Build on what outlasts the sky."},
{q:"Who knows the day and hour of his coming?", options:["No man knows, no, not the angels of heaven, but the Father only","The prophets of old","The twelve apostles","Every watchful believer"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:36",verse:"But of that day and hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels of heaven, but my Father only.", insight:"The date rests with the Father alone; date-setters contradict Christ himself."},
{q:"Why must we be always ready?", options:["For in such an hour as ye think not the Son of man cometh","For the temple will fall first","For all the signs are fulfilled","For the angels have sounded"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 24:44",verse:"Therefore be ye also ready: for in such an hour as ye think not the Son of man cometh.", insight:"He comes when we think not; readiness is the only schedule that works."}
]},
{n:25, name:"The Ten Virgins",
 seal:{ref:"Matthew 25:40",verse:"And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me."},
 facts:["Did you know a talent was an enormous sum, roughly twenty years' wages for a laborer, so even the 'one talent' servant was entrusted with a fortune (Matthew 25:15)?","Did you know 'outer darkness' with 'weeping and gnashing of teeth' appears three times in Matthew, always marking final exclusion from the kingdom (Matthew 25:30; see also 8:12 and 22:13)?","Did you know the midnight cry and the shut door echo real wedding customs, where the bridegroom's arrival hour was genuinely uncertain and latecomers truly were locked out (Matthew 25:6-10)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"To what is the kingdom of heaven likened at the chapter's opening?", options:["Ten virgins, which took their lamps, and went forth to meet the bridegroom","A wedding feast for a king's son","A net cast into the sea","A field of wheat and tares"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:1",verse:"Then shall the kingdom of heaven be likened unto ten virgins, which took their lamps, and went forth to meet the bridegroom.", insight:"Ten lamps, one bridegroom; the kingdom is about being ready for his arrival."},
{q:"How were the ten virgins divided?", options:["Five were wise, and five were foolish","Seven were wise, and three foolish","All were wise but slow","Nine were ready, and one was late"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:2",verse:"And five of them were wise, and five were foolish.", insight:"Half and half in the same company; nearness to the wise does not make us wise."},
{q:"What was the foolish virgins' mistake?", options:["They took their lamps, and took no oil with them","They forgot their lamps entirely","They slept through the night","They went to the wrong house"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:3",verse:"They that were foolish took their lamps, and took no oil with them:", insight:"Lamps without oil look right until night falls; appearance cannot substitute for inward supply."},
{q:"What did the wise virgins do differently?", options:["They took oil in their vessels with their lamps","They stayed awake all night","They hired extra servants","They kindled a bonfire"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:4",verse:"But the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps.", insight:"Vessels of oil, prepared beforehand; readiness is stocked before the crisis."},
{q:"When was the cry made, 'Behold, the bridegroom cometh'?", options:["At midnight","At evening","At dawn","At noon"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:6",verse:"And at midnight there was a cry made, Behold, the bridegroom cometh; go ye out to meet him.", insight:"Midnight, the least expected hour; his coming interrupts our sleep, not our plans."},
{q:"Why could the wise virgins not share their oil?", options:["Lest there be not enough for us and you; go ye rather to them that sell, and buy","The bridegroom had forbidden it","Their vessels were sealed shut","The oil had been borrowed"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:9",verse:"But the wise answered, saying, Not so; lest there be not enough for us and you: but go ye rather to them that sell, and buy for yourselves.", insight:"Some things cannot be borrowed; each heart must carry its own oil."},
{q:"What happened while the foolish virgins went to buy oil?", options:["The bridegroom came, they that were ready went in, and the door was shut","The wedding was postponed a day","The wise virgins fell asleep again","The lamps were all relit"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:10",verse:"And while they went to buy, the bridegroom came; and they that were ready went in with him to the marriage: and the door was shut.", insight:"The shut door is the parable's terror; opportunity has an expiry."},
{q:"What did the bridegroom say to the late virgins?", options:["Verily I say unto you, I know you not","Enter, but sit at the last place","Buy your oil and return quickly","Wait outside until morning"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:12",verse:"But he answered and said, Verily I say unto you, I know you not.", insight:"'I know you not' is the saddest sentence; standing with the company is not knowing Christ."},
{q:"How did Jesus close the parable of the virgins?", options:["Watch therefore, for ye know neither the day nor the hour wherein the Son of man cometh","Be wise as serpents and harmless as doves","The first shall be last","Many are called, but few are chosen"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:13",verse:"Watch therefore, for ye know neither the day nor the hour wherein the Son of man cometh.", insight:"Watchfulness is the moral; we prepare for an unknown hour by a known faithfulness."},
{q:"How did the man travelling into a far country divide his goods?", options:["Unto one he gave five talents, to another two, and to another one, to every man according to his several ability","Equally, one talent to each","All to the eldest servant","By casting lots"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:15",verse:"And unto one he gave five talents, to another two, and to another one; to every man according to his several ability; and straightway took his journey.", insight:"Different amounts, same trust; God measures faithfulness, not the size of the gift."},
{q:"What did the servant with five talents do?", options:["He went and traded with the same, and made them other five talents","He buried them for safety","He gave them to the poor","He returned them at once"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:16",verse:"Then he that had received the five talents went and traded with the same, and made them other five talents.", insight:"Trading takes risk; faithfulness with God's gifts is active, not cautious."},
{q:"What did the servant with one talent do?", options:["He went and digged in the earth, and hid his lord's money","He spent it on merchandise","He lent it to his fellowservants","He lost it on a journey"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:18",verse:"But he that had received one went and digged in the earth, and hid his lord’s money.", insight:"Buried treasure helps no one; unused gifts accuse the one who hides them."},
{q:"What did the lord say to the faithful servant?", options:["Well done, thou good and faithful servant: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord","Take thy rest, for thou hast done enough","Keep what thou hast gained","Sit with me upon my throne"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:21",verse:"His lord said unto him, Well done, thou good and faithful servant: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.", insight:"'Well done' is the ambition of every servant; faithfulness over little leads to joy over much."},
{q:"How did the one-talent servant describe his lord?", options:["An hard man, reaping where thou hast not sown, and gathering where thou hast not strawed","A merciful master, slow to anger","A careless lord, forgetting his goods","A generous giver, asking nothing"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:24",verse:"Then he which had received the one talent came and said, Lord, I knew thee that thou art an hard man, reaping where thou hast not sown, and gathering where thou hast not strawed:", insight:"He blamed his master's character for his own sloth; a wrong view of God excuses a wasted life."},
{q:"What did the lord call the one-talent servant?", options:["Thou wicked and slothful servant","Thou faithless and fearful servant","Thou unprofitable hireling","Thou blind and foolish man"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:26",verse:"His lord answered and said unto him, Thou wicked and slothful servant, thou knewest that I reap where I sowed not, and gather where I have not strawed:", insight:"Wicked and slothful; fear that buries the gift is judged as rebellion."},
{q:"What should the servant at least have done with the money?", options:["Put it to the exchangers, that the lord might receive his own with usury","Given it to the poor","Kept it safe in the house","Doubled it by trading"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:27",verse:"Thou oughtest therefore to have put my money to the exchangers, and then at my coming I should have received mine own with usury.", insight:"Even the smallest effort was expected; God asks for faithfulness, not brilliance."},
{q:"Where was the unprofitable servant cast?", options:["Into outer darkness, where there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth","Into the prison of the city","Out of the master's house","Into the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:30",verse:"And cast ye the unprofitable servant into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.", insight:"Uselessness has an end; outer darkness is the portion of wasted grace."},
{q:"How will the Son of man separate the nations?", options:["As a shepherd divideth his sheep from the goats","As a farmer separates wheat from tares","As a fisherman sorts the catch","As a king divides the spoil"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:32",verse:"And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another, as a shepherd divideth his sheep from the goats:", insight:"Sheep and goats graze together until the shepherd comes; the separating is his work, not ours."},
{q:"What will the King say to those on his right hand?", options:["Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world","Enter thou into the joy of thy lord","Well done, good and faithful servant","Sit with me upon my throne"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:34",verse:"Then shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:", insight:"The kingdom was prepared before the world began; our welcome was planned before our birth."},
{q:"How did the King measure their kindness to the needy?", options:["Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me","By the number of their good deeds","By the size of their gifts","By their prayers in secret"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 25:40",verse:"And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.", insight:"A kindness to the least is done to Christ; no mercy is too small to reach heaven."}
]}
]);
